cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Governança de Verificação em Sistemas de Agentes LLM: tratando a saída do agente com o ceticismo da integração contínua"
message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Fernandes
    given-names: Ted
    email: tedfernandes@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7522-326X"
abstract: >-
  Multi-agent LLM frameworks have converged on a company-of-agents organization, but
  under-address how such systems verify their own output and avoid reporting success when
  nothing was checked. This experience report describes a production agent system whose
  distinguishing contribution is a verification substrate: an explicit indeterminate outcome
  state, an LLM-free defect-ledger ratchet of provenance-linked invariants that prefer executing
  artifacts over string-matching them, a loop that compiles each confirmed defect into an
  enforced check, property-based prompt-change regression gates, and untrusted-by-default handling
  of agent-authored context.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - multi-agent systems
  - software engineering
  - verification
  - evaluation
  - agent governance
  - experience report
